---@class cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecord
---@field id string Identifier.
---@field name string Complete DNS record name, including the zone name, in Punycode.
---@field ttl number Time To Live (TTL) of the DNS record in seconds. Setting to 1 means 'automatic'. Value must be between 60 and 86400, with the minimum reduced to 30 for Enterprise zones.
---@field type cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecordType|string Record type.
---@field comment? string Comments or notes about the DNS record. This field has no effect on DNS responses.
---@field content? string A single Base64-encoded OpenPGP Transferable Public Key (RFC 4880 Section 11.1)
---@field proxied? boolean Whether the record is receiving the performance and security benefits of Cloudflare.
---@field settings? cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecordSettings Settings for the DNS record.
---@field tags? cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecordTagsList Custom tags for the DNS record. This field has no effect on DNS responses.

---@class cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecordSettings
---@field ipv4_only? boolean When enabled, only A records will be generated, and AAAA records will not be created. This setting is intended for exceptional cases. Note that this option only applies to proxied records and it has no effect on whether Cloudflare communicates with the origin using IPv4 or IPv6.
---@field ipv6_only? boolean When enabled, only AAAA records will be generated, and A records will not be created. This setting is intended for exceptional cases. Note that this option only applies to proxied records and it has no effect on whether Cloudflare communicates with the origin using IPv4 or IPv6.

---@alias cloudflare.dns.RecordsBatchRequestPutsItemOpenpgpkeyRecordTagsList string[]

