---@class cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaults
---@field flatten_all_cnames? boolean Whether to flatten all CNAME records in the zone. Note that, due to DNS limitations, a CNAME record at the zone apex will always be flattened.
---@field internal_dns? cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsInternalDns Settings for this internal zone.
---@field multi_provider? boolean Whether to enable multi-provider DNS, which causes Cloudflare to activate the zone even when non-Cloudflare NS records exist, and to respect NS records at the zone apex during outbound zone transfers.
---@field nameservers? cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsNameservers Settings determining the nameservers through which the zone should be available.
---@field ns_ttl? number The time to live (TTL) of the zone's nameserver (NS) records.
---@field secondary_overrides? boolean Allows a Secondary DNS zone to use (proxied) override records and CNAME flattening at the zone apex.
---@field soa? cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsSoa Components of the zone's SOA record.
---@field zone_mode? cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsZoneMode|string Whether the zone mode is a regular or CDN/DNS only zone.

---@class cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsInternalDns
---@field reference_zone_id? string The ID of the zone to fallback to.

---@class cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsNameservers
---@field type? cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsNameserversType|string Nameserver type

---@alias cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsNameserversType "cloudflare.standard"|"cloudflare.advanced"|"cloudflare.standard.random"|"custom.account"|"custom.tenant"

---@class cloudflare.dns.SettingsAccountEditRequestZoneDefaultsSoa
---@field expire? number Time in seconds of being unable to query the primary server after which secondary servers should stop serving the zone.
---@field min_ttl? number The time to live (TTL) for negative caching of records within the zone.
---@field mname? string The primary nameserver, which may be used for outbound zone transfers. If null, a Cloudflare-assigned value will be used.
---@field refresh? number Time in seconds after which secondary servers should re-check the SOA record to see if the zone has been updated.
---@field retry? number Time in seconds after which secondary servers should retry queries after the primary server was unresponsive.
